+### Biome Height Shapers
+Biome-specific height generation functions using 2D noise or sine/cosine waves to create distinct terrain profiles for different biomes [S5, unofficial].
+**Formulas:**
+- Plains height: $h = (1 \cdot N_1(x,y) + 0.25 \cdot N_2(x,y)) \cdot 8 + 15$, where $N_1$ is noise at scale 0.005 and $N_2$ at scale 0.02 [S5, unofficial].
+- Mountain height (ridged noise): $n1 = 1 - |2N_1 - 1|$, $n2 = 1 - |2N_2 - 1|$, $h = (n1^2 + 0.5 \cdot n2^2) \cdot 35 + 15$, where $N_1$ is noise at scale 0.008 and $N_2$ at scale 0.02 [S5, unofficial].
+- Desert height (dunes): $h = |\sin(x \cdot 0.02 + N_1(x,y) \cdot 2) \cdot \cos(z \cdot 0.02)| \cdot 10 + 14$, where $N_1$ is noise at scale 0.01 [S5, unofficial].
